# This is the processing directive for concurrent-reliance-temporal Anchor Modeling in Vertica
#
# The templates are in the Sisula language (docs/SISULA.md) and render the JSON bindings that the
# modeler builds (Generate > JSON bindings). The scripts first in the list prepare the schema that the
# bindings are made from; they run once, before the templates. A line starting with # is not run.
#
# Vertica has no function that returns a table, so the rewinders are views of what is known now, and of the perspectives
# only the latest and the now perspectives are made, for each positor. It has no triggers either.
SQL/Helpers.js
SQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Vertica/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Vertica/derive.js
SQL/Vertica/CreateSchemas.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreatePositorAndDefault.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateKnots.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateAnchors.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateNexuses.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateAttributes.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateAttributeAssembledViews.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateAttributeRewinders.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateAnchorPerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateNexusPerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateTies.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateTieAssembledViews.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateTieRewinders.sisula
SQL/Vertica/crt/CreateTiePerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/AddDescriptions.sisula
